# Core Project Standards

- **Package manager:** Use `pnpm` (and `pnpm dlx` for one-off CLIs). Do not use npm or yarn.
- **TypeScript:** Prefer `unknown` with type guards or Zod over `any`. Do not add `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` unless unavoidable and documented. Avoid new non-null assertions (`!`); narrow instead.
- **Imports:** Use explicit type imports (`import type { Foo } from './bar'`). Prefer named exports; default exports only where Astro pages/layouts require them.
- **Boundaries:** Keep business logic out of HTTP handlers, UI markup, and DB driver wiring when a shared package already owns it (`packages/api`, `packages/db`, `packages/auth`).
- **Completeness:** Ship runnable code—no `// TODO` stubs or truncated implementations in edited files.
